{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/543393-sidereals-less-fate-more-ninja","id":543393,"title":"Sidereals, less fate more ninja","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-06T20:00:12-07:00","id":543393,"title":"Sidereals, less fate more ninja","content":"This is a new idea I am trying out in my current game. Basically, sidereals are not employees in the Bureaucracy of Yu-shan. They hold no official office, instead they are mercenaries contracted by the bureaucracy or specific gods. The higher ups are more like guild masters, facilitating relationships between Yu-Shan and organizing missions that require multiple sidereals. A few advantages to this. Storywise it makes it much easier to justify characters doing as they like. Its pretty rare player characters hold an office so they dont lose much. While it opens up working for gods in other areas. The god of gambling is concerned about some statistically improbably lucky streaks, god of libraries is having trouble locating a specific book, etc.<br /> <br /> Added bonus of applying arcane fate to the celestial bureaucracy. They cannot hold an official position nor can there be any record of their activities. Which is precisely why they are used. They are like the real world historical ninja. Using them when you want something done off the record. When you dont want anyone to know or atleast need rather specialized skills. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T21:14:11-07:00","id":543455,"title":"","content":"That definitely sounds like an interesting sort of take on them. Makes it a very different style of game, but I can see it being fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T01:41:51-07:00","id":543626,"title":"","content":"I like extending the curse of the broken Mask to Yu-Shan. Sounds good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5706-zeal","name":"Zeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T07:37:02-07:00","id":543887,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting idea - I would generally prefer Sidereals who were more connected to the world and had more personal discretion in how they operate, but it's a different take.<br /> <br /> My first question would be what is the payment here? Are these mercenaries for money, or are they seeking favours or what? If they do seek money or favours, does it make sense for them to do that via hiring themselves out for missions rather than politics, trade, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T21:30:20-07:00","id":562612,"title":"","content":"I like this idea! Personally, I would tweak it a bit, so that the Sids DO have &quot;day jobs&quot; at the Bureau of Destiny, but this just gives them an official reason to be in Heaven; really, Gods do most of the scut work that Sids canonically do, while they &quot;Clark Kent&quot; these roles. <br /> <br /> What I really like about this take is that it allows the Sids to interact and work with Gods other than in the B. of Destiny, carrying out missions for the other Bureaus, even working for the criminal gods in the heavenly slums. And there's no reason Sidereal elders can't arrange for missions for the Gods of the Terrestrial Bureaucracy, as well...Of course, this can lead to direct conflict with Exigents...<br /> <br /> Kudos for such an intriguing take on the splat!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}